To modify your Spring MVC setup to allow a date field to be nullable (i.e., accepting blank input), you will need to customize your date formatter slightly. In Spring, you can create a custom formatter that extends `DateFormatter` to override the default behavior and return `null` when an empty string is encountered.

Here's how you can define a custom date formatter to handle null values:

```java
import org.springframework.format.datetime.DateFormatter;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class CustomDateFormatter extends DateFormatter {

    @Override
    public Date parse(String text, Locale locale) throws ParseException {
        if (text == null || text.trim().isEmpty()) {
            return null; // Allow blank input to return null
        }
        return super.parse(text, locale); // Call the parent class's parse method for other cases
    }
}
```

